    <briefdescription>
<para>Runtime of the DSHL render_pass objects. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A render_pass declared in DSHL is a shape: targets, subpasses, reads, resolves and the framebuffer layouts it supports, stored in the shader dump. This API turns a shape into a live d3d render pass and drives it. Shapes and layouts are looked up in the main dump only. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
